  CURVE_X_RANGE            = (0, 10)      TI=new F(0,10),CI=TI.getLength(),xI=.1*CI,EI=CI*xI;
  TYPICAL_Y                = 1
  numberOfPoints           = 1251   -> dx = 0.0080000000000000002
  smoothingStandardDeviation = 0.050000000000000003   (0.005 x the x range)
  edgeSlopeFactor          = 0.40000000000000002   (0.04 x the x range)
  maxTilt                  = 25
  CURVE_MANIPULATION_WIDTH_RANGE = [1, 5] default 2
  CURVE_MANIPULATION_Y_RANGE     = (-2, 2)
  SLOPE_OF_TANGENT_MODEL_RANGE   = (-8, 8)
  NET_SIGNED_AREA_MODEL_RANGE    = (-8, 8)
  MAX_UNDO                 = 20
  freeform click width     = 0.25
  hill Gaussian      Math.exp(-Math.pow((t.x-r.x)/(e/(2*Math.sqrt(2))),2))
  triangle slope     s=DR/(e/2)
  parabola curv.     s=DR*Math.pow(2/e,2)
  pedestal quartic   Math.exp(-1*((e-t)/xR)**4)
  pedestal plateau   s=e-2*xR
  sinusoid period    2*Math.PI*e/kI.CURVE_MANIPULATION_WIDTH_RANGE.defaultValue
  sinusoid extent    o=n/2*7,a=n/8
  sinusoid taper     Math.cos(Math.PI/2*(e.x-t)/Math.abs(i-t))**2
  blend threshold    e.y=t>1e-8?t*i+(1-t)*e.lastSavedY:e.lastSavedY
  smooth type        e.pointType=t>.999?"smooth"
  smooth kernel      1/(ER*Math.sqrt(2*Math.PI))
  smooth window      for(let n=this.deltaX;n<=3*ER;n+=this.deltaX)
  region-zero tol    Math.abs(i.lastSavedY)<.001
  PhET derivative    "number"==typeof i&&"number"==typeof r?this.points[n].y=(i+r)/2
  PhET integral      .5*(t.y+i.y)*(t.x-i.x)
  PhET 2nd deriv     (r.getSlope(n)-r.getSlope(t))/this.deltaX

=== B1  the fundamental theorem on the grid ===
  max |int(f') - (f - f(0))|              = 4.885e-15   (6 random curves)
  max |d/dx int(g) - g|                   = 1.643e-14
  max |d/dx trap(f) - (f[i]+f[i+1])/2|    = 7.105e-15
  -> the two operators are inverse to each other in floating point,
     and the "value" the derivative of the integral returns is f at the
     cell midpoint -- which is EXACT for a piecewise-linear curve, not
     an approximation (the mean value theorem, with the mean value
     sitting at the midpoint of a straight segment).

=== B2  PhET's pair is not exactly inverse: the [1,2,1]/4 identity ===
  max |D_central(I_trap(f))[i] - (f[i-1]+2f[i]+f[i+1])/4| = 6.217e-15
  So PhET's central difference of its trapezium integral returns the
  [1,2,1]/4 smoothing of f, not f.  The difference is O(dx^2 f") and is
  invisible on its graphs; it is named here because this remake chose the
  staggered pair instead, for which the theorem is exact.

=== B3  the five analytic modes against their closed forms ===
  dx = 0.008.  The cell derivative is the EXACT derivative of the drawn
  piecewise-linear curve; against the SMOOTH shape it carries the
  Euler-Maclaurin term g'''(x) dx^2/24, and the trapezium integral carries
  -(g'(b) - g'(a)) dx^2/12.  Both are measured, not assumed.
  hill      w=2.00 x0=3.00 y=+1.50 :  max|f'-g'| = 4.416e-05   max|F-G| = 9.704e-06
  triangle  w=2.00 x0=4.00 y=+1.50 :  max|f'-g'| = 1.101e-13   max|F-G| = 1.600e-05
  pedestal: closed form (incomplete gamma) vs quadrature: 1.67e-15
  pedestal  w=3.00 x0=5.00 y=+1.20 :  max|f'-g'| = 1.070e-03   max|F-G| = 2.437e-05
  parabola  w=2.50 x0=6.00 y=-1.40 :  max|f'-g'| = 1.708e-13   max|F-G| = 1.353e-05
  sinusoid  w=2.00 x0=5.00 y=+1.00 :  max|f'-g'| = 2.667e-06   max|F-G| = 1.045e-05

  the triangle and the parabola are special:
    triangle  (piecewise LINEAR): derivative exact to 1.10e-13
    its integral is the EXACT integral of the drawn curve; against the
    ideal triangle it differs by 1.600e-05, which is not a quadrature error at
    all but the two junction cells: the sampled curve runs to zero over a
    whole cell instead of stopping at the junction, worth s d (dx - d) / 2
    per junction, at most 2 x s dx^2 / 8 = 1.600e-05.
    parabola  (QUADRATIC): the cell derivative is exact to 1.71e-13,
              and over [5.400, 6.400] its trapezium error is 6.826667e-06
              against the Euler-Maclaurin term +dx^2/12 (g'(b)-g'(a)) = 6.826667e-06
              difference 7.067e-16  -- the expansion TERMINATES for a quadratic

=== B4  the discretisation error is O(dx^2): halve dx, quarter the error ===
  hill      errors 4.416e-05 1.104e-05 2.760e-06 6.901e-07   ratios 4.000 4.000 4.000
  sinusoid  errors 2.667e-06 6.667e-07 1.667e-07 4.167e-08   ratios 4.000 4.000 4.000
  pedestal  errors 1.070e-03 2.676e-04 6.690e-05 1.673e-05   ratios 3.999 3.999 4.000

=== B5  corners, and the one-sided limits ===
  triangle, w = 2, apex at x = 4.000, height 1.50
    slope of the cell just LEFT of the apex   = +1.0000000000000009
    slope of the cell just RIGHT of the apex  = -1.0000000000000009
    closed form  +/- TYPICAL_Y/(w/2)          = +1
    the two one-sided limits differ by 2; no value exists at the apex.
    integral of f" over 81 nodes about the apex = -2.0000000000000018
    = slope(right cell) - slope(left cell) = -2.0000000000000018  (exact: telescoping)
    the junctions sit at x = 2.50000 and 5.50000 (y/s from the apex)
    there the slope jumps from +1.0000 to 0 and from -1.0000 to 0
  parabola, w = 2.5, vertex at x = 6.000, depth -1.40
    the vertex is SMOOTH (slope 0); the corners are at the junctions
    x = 4.52098 and 7.47902, where the slope jumps by 1.8931455305918772
    measured jump across the left junction  = 1.8790399999999985
    (short of the closed form by 0.0141: the junction falls INSIDE a cell,
     so the nearest clean cell is ~1.5 dx in and the parabola's slope
     there is already 2 s (1.5 dx) = 0.0154 smaller.  A corner's position
     is only known to one cell; its one-sided LIMITS are not.)
  sinusoid on an EMPTY curve: PhET drops the taper when the region it
    would blend into is zero, so the packet ends in two corners at
    x = -5.99557 and 15.99557, each a slope jump of 1
  hill and pedestal have NO corner:
    hill      max |slope change between neighbouring cells| = 4.800e-02
    pedestal  max |slope change between neighbouring cells| = 2.295e-01
    (PhET calls them "smooth transitions"; the pedestal join is C3 -- the
     quartic exp(-u^4) has value 1 and zero first, second and third
     derivatives at u = 0, so only f"" jumps there.)

