=== B6  the tangent tool and the area tool, by independent routes ===
  tangent slope == the derivative curve at the same x, worst 0.00e+00 over 10 x
  and the drawn tangent line passes through both nodes of its cell exactly.
  net signed area (split at every zero crossing) == the integral curve,
  worst 2.78e-16 over 8 endpoints.
  over the whole range the default curve has  +2.0052864004760713  -1.7279999999999998  net 0.27728640047607156

=== B7  PhET's smoothing operator ===
  kernel: Gaussian sigma = 0.05, truncated at 3 sigma, sampled every dx
  -> 18 taps each side (3 sigma / dx = 18.750)
  a constant is preserved to 4.44e-16 (the weights are renormalised)
  peak weight 1/(sigma sqrt(2 pi)) = 7.9788456080286538, weights sum to 124.61937531282095
  a hill of width 2 (a Gaussian of sd w/4 = 0.5) smoothed:
    peak 1.5 -> 1.4927703895473889   (ratio 0.9951802596982593)
    an untruncated Gaussian kernel would give sd sqrt(0.5^2 + 0.05^2) = 0.50249378,
    so a peak ratio of 0.99503719; the truncated, renormalised, sampled kernel
    gives 0.99518026 -- the difference is the truncation, and it is measured.
    the area is preserved to 2.220e-16
  a triangle apex, smoothed: the cell slopes either side of the apex go
    from +1.000000 / -1.000000 to +0.064026 / -0.064026
    the corner is rounded over about 6 sigma = 0.300 in x

=== B8  tilt and shift ===
  tilt: pinned at the left edge, so f(0) is unchanged: 0.000e+00
        and the dragged point lands exactly on the pointer: 0.000e+00
        every cell slope changes by the same amount, spread 7.144e-14
  tilt refuses a slope of magnitude 25 or more (PhET's maxTilt)
        a drag to (0.04, 2.0) asks for slope 50.0 -> refused: True
  shift: the whole curve moves rigidly; every slope is unchanged: 2.776e-14
         (not 0: a slope is a difference of order-1 numbers divided by
          dx = 0.008, so one ulp of f is 2.9e-14 of slope)
         and the integral gains exactly delta * x: 2.096e-13

=== B9  erf: the series the JS uses, against scipy ===
  max |erf_series - scipy.special.erf| over -6..6 = 1.443e-15

=== B10  numbers the views print ===
  the file opens with a hill (w 2.0, x 3.2, y +1.6) then a triangle
  (w 2.4, x 6.8, y -1.2) laid on an empty curve, because a flat curve
  makes every one of these views blank.  PhET opens flat; "erase" here
  gives exactly that.
